. local present : list a | b

. local miss : list all - present

. display "employees in the window: " `: word count `present'' ", added as isolate
> s: " `: word count `miss''
employees in the window: 102, added as isolates: 42

. nwset sender receiver, directed eventtime(t) name(mail)

. local miss : subinstr local miss " " ",", all

. nwaddnodes mail, nodenames(`miss')

. nwset
(1 networks)
--------------------
      mail

. 
. * --- five specifications ---
. quietly nwrem mail, nodsnd nidrec

. estimates store m1

. quietly nwrem mail, frpsndsnd frrecsnd

. estimates store m2

. quietly nwrem mail, nodsnd nidrec frpsndsnd frrecsnd

. estimates store m3

. quietly nwrem mail, rsndsnd rrecsnd

. estimates store m4

. quietly nwrem mail, nodsnd nidrec rsndsnd rrecsnd

. estimates store m5

. 
. * --- compare: log likelihood, number of parameters, AIC and BIC ---
. estimates stats m1 m2 m3 m4 m5

Akaike's information criterion and Bayesian information criterion

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
       Model |          N   ll(null)  ll(model)      df        AIC        BIC
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------------
          m1 |        631          .  -5992.517       2   11989.03   11997.93
          m2 |        631          .  -5733.442       2   11470.88   11479.78
          m3 |        631          .  -5531.783       4   11071.57   11089.36
          m4 |        631          .  -5389.231       2   10782.46   10791.36
          m5 |        631          .  -5221.696       4   10451.39   10469.18
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note: BIC uses N = number of observations. See [R] BIC note.

. lrtest m3 m1

Likelihood-ratio test
Assumption: m1 nested within m3

 LR chi2(2) = 921.47
Prob > chi2 = 0.0000

. lrtest m3 m2

Likelihood-ratio test
Assumption: m2 nested within m3

 LR chi2(2) = 403.32
Prob > chi2 = 0.0000

